On 10/18/05 5:47 PM, james wrote:
> Air Elementals on the Plane of Air (who have taken a
> character of mine from 1200 HP down to 300 in a handful of rounds.)

Air elementals can be effectively dealt with in one turn by wands of 
death, polymorph, or (less permanently) teleport; conflict is also very 
helpful on Air; and potions of full healing ingested at the right times 
can be very helpful.

I admit I've had some harrowing times on Air; nonetheless, I've been 
across that Plane about eight times or so, never died, and I don't think 
I ever had more than 300 HP doing so.

Put it this way: the blessed potion of full healing that adds 8 hp to 
your max while you're trying to beef up could give you up to 400 hp 
while you're in trouble. It doesn't make sense to quaff all of them 
immediately after alchemizing them. Save some for emergencies, and your 
300 hp character can *effectively* have several times that much.

